    <item>
     <DOKIL>
      <ID>FU</ID>
      <OBJECT>ZFPM_ALM_PM_NOTIF_CREATE</OBJECT>
      <LANGU>E</LANGU>
      <TYP>T</TYP>
      <VERSION>0009</VERSION>
      <MASTERLANG>X</MASTERLANG>
      <TXTLINES>00028</TXTLINES>
      <DOKSTATE>A</DOKSTATE>
     </DOKIL>
     <HEAD>
      <TDOBJECT>DOKU</TDOBJECT>
      <TDNAME>ZFPM_ALM_PM_NOTIF_CREATE</TDNAME>
      <TDID>FU</TDID>
      <TDSPRAS>E</TDSPRAS>
      <TDFORM>S_DOCU_SHOW</TDFORM>
      <TDSTYLE>S_DOCUS1</TDSTYLE>
      <TDVERSION>00009</TDVERSION>
      <TDLINESIZE>072</TDLINESIZE>
     </HEAD>
     <LINES>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Functionality</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>This BAPI enables you to create a new service notification. This allows</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>you to create certain fields from the notification header, items,</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>causes, tasks, activities and also long texts for them. Partners can</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>also be maintained.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Notes</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Errors are returned in the parameter RETURN.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Technical note</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>The sort field must be filled in order to create items, causes, task or</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>activities. When creating a cause the sort field for the item must also</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>be filled.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>When creating a long text the fields OBJTYP and OBJKEY must be filled.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>OBJTYP can contain the following values:</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>N1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>QMEL - notification header</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>N1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>QMFE - notification item</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>N1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>QMUR - notification cause</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>N1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>QMSM - notification task</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>N1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>QMMA - notification activity</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>OBJKEY must contain the corresponding sort field for the above values.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>The combination of sort field item/cause, item/task or item/activity</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>must be unique within the same notification. If you leave the sort field</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>blank and OBJTYP = QMEL, the long text is created for the notification</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>header.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>An external reference key can be transferred by the field REFOBJECTKEY.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>The links between external reference keys &lt;-&gt; SAP keys are returned</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>within export table KEY_RELATIONSHIPS. If the fields SENDER,</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>REFOBJECTTYPE and REFRELTYPE are filled, it is possible to create an</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>object link at notification header level.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
     </LINES>
    </item>
